From 83826fc05ee244b4a29cecd5ef684ad635f0279c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:04:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] drm/lima: cancel a pending heap recovery in the timeout
 handler
To: Qiang Yu <yuq825@gmail.com>
Cc: Erico Nunes <nunes.erico@gmail.com>,
    Danilo Krummrich <dakr@kernel.org>,
    Maarten Lankhorst <maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com>,
    Maxime Ripard <mripard@kernel.org>,
    Thomas Zimmermann <tzimmermann@suse.de>,
    David Airlie <airlied@gmail.com>,
    Simona Vetter <simona@ffwll.ch>,
    lima@lists.freedesktop.org,
    dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

An out-of-heap interrupt queues pipe->recover_work. If the job then
fails for another reason (an MMU page fault or the scheduler timeout)
before the work runs, the timeout handler resets the core and clears
pipe->current_task, and the work later runs lima_gp_task_recover() on
the idle core: it dereferences the NULL current_task and restarts the
PLBU allocation of a job that no longer exists.

After masking the irqs, wait for a handler that may still queue the
work, cancel the work, and mask the irqs again, since a recovery that
was already running unmasks the GP irqs and restarts the PLBU.

Found by review; this race has not been observed on hardware.

Fixes: 2081e8dcf1ee ("drm/lima: recover task by enlarging heap buffer")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
index 7e7df5c8a9d..07d2f82ae08 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
@@ -436,6 +436,17 @@ static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat lima_sched_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *job
 	 */
 	pipe->task_mask_irq(pipe);
 
+	/*
+	 * A heap recovery queued before the error must not run on the reset
+	 * core. An irq handler that started before the mask may still queue
+	 * it, and a running one unmasks the GP irqs again: wait for both,
+	 * then mask once more.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_processor; i++)
+		synchronize_irq(pipe->processor[i]->irq);
+	cancel_work_sync(&pipe->recover_work);
+	pipe->task_mask_irq(pipe);
+
 	if (!pipe->error)
 		DRM_ERROR("%s job timeout\n", lima_ip_name(ip));
 
-- 
